The audience is first-time, never-licensed applicants for a Michigan operator's license, reading at a plain-English level, plus newcomers and parents of teen drivers who use the same handbook. This section covers school bus light signals, yielding when turning and at intersections including four-way stops and malfunctioning signals, yielding to pedestrians and funeral processions, and the rules for passing on the left, passing on the right and when passing is prohibited. It teaches what each school bus light requires, who goes first at intersections, when drivers must yield to pedestrians, and when and how passing is allowed. It assumes no prior driving knowledge and no prerequisites beyond literacy, so wording stays concrete, procedural and free of legal jargon throughout.
